cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >
  If you use or reference this experiment, please cite it using the metadata
  in this file.
type: software
title: >
  plateau-mago-implicit: Implicit 3D Tiles from Project PLATEAU CityGML
  using Mago 3DTiler
abstract: >
  A small, rigorous, reproducible technical experiment testing whether building
  data from Project PLATEAU CityGML for Muroran City (室蘭市) and Sarabetsu
  Village (更別村) can be converted into Implicit 3D Tiles using Mago 3DTiler
  in a deterministic and reproducible manner, and consumed comfortably with
  CesiumJS from ordinary static HTTP storage. Presented in the working style
  of UN Open GIS Initiative DWG7.
repository-code: https://github.com/dwg7/plateau-mago-implicit
license: CC0-1.0
keywords:
  - 3D Tiles
  - Implicit Tiling
  - CityGML
  - Project PLATEAU
  - Mago 3DTiler
  - CesiumJS
  - reproducibility
  - determinism
  - static delivery
  - open source
  - UN Open GIS Initiative
  - DWG7
  - Muroran
  - Sarabetsu
